llowers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xunit/xunit/issues/comments/2730620630","html_url":"https://github.com/xunit/xunit/issues/3213#issuecomment-2730620630","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xunit/xunit/issues/3213","id":2730620630,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAJbtsc6iwfbW","user":{"login":"bradwilson","id":16944,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2OTQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16944?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson","html_url":"https://github.com/bradwilson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-17T19:33:42Z","updated_at":"2025-03-17T19:33:42Z","body":"The best I can do right now is \"double report\" the test result: one passing, one failing, for any affected test.\n\nThis is what the command line MTP looks like:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/91abdf32-fa79-4e0e-afeb-dad6f3ef74c9)\n\nAnd this is what Visual Studio looks like:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4b2e4dd4-71c2-4ee7-a85d-658500d2ea04)\n\nThe downside is that it's reported as a failure for every affected test, so if I add a second test to the test class, this is the result:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f4e7d7eb-cf66-4fa0-bf4f-a97be97021bd)\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ae3f3ab8-ab3b-4713-9b5f-fb009f968a5b)\n\nThis \"multiplication of failures\" gets worse as you go further up (collection fixtures would fail every test in the collection, and assembly fixtures would fail every test in the assembly).\n\nGiven that it's an architectural discussion in MTP to decide how/when to surface these kinds of things, there's not much else that can be done on our side until an MTP alternative (that supports Test Explorer) is available. On the whole, though, this seems better than ignoring them.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xunit/xunit/issues/comments/2730620630/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"bradwilson","id":16944,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2OTQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16944?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson","html_url":"https://github.com/bradwilson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradwilson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_